820332c07c597cb963b36a5bbef55f6cf.svg) | ![](images/95/95836ae470c61ab15bfb67d6f0c92d2ad8d03d400b04473e81e58de3ee44bf32.svg) | ![](images/37/37e17c4a2302e6352fb7186621c9c43bb5e99d43a8a0bc700c0181d36c6cc915.svg) | ![](images/46/46908fb7561d19927fe58a38ab26cba3ff8a35cf75cc0da234f08773dc991398.svg) |\n|  | ![](images/95/95836ae470c61ab15bfb67d6f0c92d2ad8d03d400b04473e81e58de3ee44bf32.svg) | ![](images/37/37e17c4a2302e6352fb7186621c9c43bb5e99d43a8a0bc700c0181d36c6cc915.svg) | ![](images/46/46908fb7561d19927fe58a38ab26cba3ff8a35cf75cc0da234f08773dc991398.svg) | ![](images/15/156b31ede73de5301befe67f02745a0202f1806a62f9fdecc6fc9ee3f21117ba.svg) |\n\nSo, we obtain the following factorization:\n![](images/d8/d802c5d6ff81a500a8d7d00ec9e20daafb07d355a1ce0d9a0b48dc03a88088c9.svg)\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ![](images/19/191f231d4e62c28931ed18cf133acb0e0ec66e845af743409198c4420953bd52.svg) ![](images/eb/eb3981cb149c9d1b26c2b87bd92a5aef5ead1787d8cb817fa3c1efd6a66074f9.svg) and ![](images/e9/e988f1ab98136f2d888e83baf436d8f659654a55eb2d2b3e11029b365a52c6e0.svg)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124380 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124571 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef311af0-0e95-5574-a151-2971ad66bd08" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 4x4 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/id #uuid "a1c51187-c0a6-505c-bc58-2319b439086e" :question/math-academy-id "e-7047" :question/problem "![](images/2e/2e17e4fa743f6f8d3f5987b9095cf6976ae8eadf36ee4456ea8a9195201526e4.svg)\n\nConsider the matrix $P$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\lambda=4$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n\nII. $\\lambda=-1$ is an eigenvalue of $P$\n\nIII. The eigenvalue $\\lambda=6$ has algebraic multiplicity $2$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\, P-\\lambda I \\mathbin{:}$\n﻿﻿﻿![](images/38/38316eff018e61b4f9f6ce90e0e231ed1eeb6fe993f3b107a5ad8057e3641fd4.svg)\n\nThe characteristic equation is $\\det(P-\\lambda I) = 0.$ \n\nNotice that we can expand the $4 \\times 4$ determinant across the $1$st column, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 0 & -8 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1-\\lambda  & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 3 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 7 & -3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, expanding the $3 \\times 3$ determinant across the $2$nd row, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3-\\lambda )\\cdot (4-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ 7 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )((-1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-35) & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-36) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -6)(\\lambda +6) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the eigenvalues of $P$ are $\\lambda=3,$ $\\lambda=4,$ $\\lambda=6,$ and $\\lambda=-6$ (all with algebraic multiplicity $1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\""}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442272 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124523 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5abea3ab-76a7-5598-8ede-b4cf88dd47d7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Eigenvalues of a General 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d0700ae-412d-51b3-a257-618c99674341" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-2,1,5\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442260} {:answer/id #uuid "481860b5-bb3d-58cb-94dc-529c4d401e99" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-5,1,3\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442261} {:answer/id #uuid "558359c6-2d82-546e-a690-6c2a868d98cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{1,2,5\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442262} {:answer/id #uuid "6819477a-eb82-5fe8-9144-a2c3b8ccd8c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-5,-1,2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442263} {:answer/id #uuid "974ccec8-a09e-54db-b466-a20773981b7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-5,1,2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442266}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "974ccec8-a09e-54db-b466-a20773981b7f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-5,1,2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442266} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8e6f41c-9e5c-55de-9517-8eaa2b14ab20" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442270}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bedee111-5fec-56ad-a271-6904f3e057b2" :question/math-academy-id "q-140475" :question/problem "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is given by $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-3-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|+(-1)|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3-\\lambda  \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+15\\lambda )+(-5-\\lambda )+(5+\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+13\\lambda -10 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +10 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to solve this equation. We find the first root by testing some values. According to the rational zeros theorem, a list of good first guesses consists of all divisors of $10:$ \n\n$$\n\\pm 1,\\pm 2,\\pm 5,\\pm 10\n$$\n\nLet's pick $x=1.$ Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1)^{3}+2(1)^{2}-13(1)+10 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =1$ is a root of the equation. So, we can factor $(\\lambda -1)$ out of ${\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +10$ using synthetic division:\n\n| $1$ | $1$ | $2$ | $-13$ | $10$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $↓$ | $1$ | $3$ | $-10$ |\n|  | $1$ | $3$ | $-10$ | $0$ |\n\nSo, we obtain the following factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda -1)({\\lambda }^{2}+3\\lambda -10) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +5)(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-5,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=1,\\,$ and $\\,{\\lambda }_{3}=2.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186272116 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124523 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5abea3ab-76a7-5598-8ede-b4cf88dd47d7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Eigenvalues of a General 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "343afa09-d3de-5a19-916a-586f7a7d1e10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda -30=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269747} {:answer/id #uuid "486477e7-c24f-5198-8b45-bd30ea74890e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}+13\\lambda -15=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186269929} {:answer/id #uuid "6228aba2-8afa-597c-95c4-f06c42a62e0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}+13{\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +4=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186270132} {:answer/id #uuid "d6af2f78-c6df-57d2-ac96-1c55af121e04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +10=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271152} {:answer/id #uuid "f703200a-d0b5-505b-8a01-4c910b8e7ab9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +25=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271436}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d6af2f78-c6df-57d2-ac96-1c55af121e04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +10=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271152} :answer-field/id #uuid "d819e362-fc4f-51eb-a589-2bd16ee43e88" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186271891}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "29164807-d381-53a4-8efb-e16c83f907bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-140515" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$C=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,C-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nC-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(C-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -3-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-3-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-(-1)|\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|+(-1)|\\begin{aligned}1 & -3-\\lambda  \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+5\\lambda )+(-\\lambda -5)-(5+\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+15\\lambda )-\\lambda -5-5-\\lambda  & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}+13\\lambda -10 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-13\\lambda +10 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125011 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124571 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef311af0-0e95-5574-a151-2971ad66bd08" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 4x4 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "414f9370-14a3-5aa6-8486-cea2e27301a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -2)^{2}(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -5)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447397} {:answer/id #uuid "457e9051-86d9-52ea-9195-8e29a88ad83f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -2)(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -5)(\\lambda -1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447398} {:answer/id #uuid "691f275b-fd9a-54d9-8586-a64a1a03045b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -2)(\\lambda -5)^{2}(\\lambda +1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447409} {:answer/id #uuid "75cdd761-23be-5c11-826b-34cb06e74a70" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -2)^{2}(\\lambda -5)^{2}=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447415} {:answer/id #uuid "8bcf654c-f10a-5880-a4ae-224b5c7e4e07" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -2)(\\lambda -5)(\\lambda +1)^{2}=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447423}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "457e9051-86d9-52ea-9195-8e29a88ad83f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -2)(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -5)(\\lambda -1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447398} :answer-field/id #uuid "34c56093-04e6-5946-b523-0fde12c0770a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186122666}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d28aed4f-dd9b-57fa-bc7d-1ecf9008bea3" :question/math-academy-id "q-36819" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 5 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1-\\lambda  & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 5 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1-\\lambda  & 5 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(-1-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -2)(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -5)(\\lambda -1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186427385 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124522 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "289ae874-f555-50ee-896f-eb2188004124" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 3x3 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0fde5085-a635-5696-9cd7-100b3c72cad2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-1,4,1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427374} {:answer/id #uuid "578c36b5-c09b-5821-8e36-ba81ab9528bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-1,-4,1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427376} {:answer/id #uuid "78e32da7-f1e3-50b7-a080-2498d2b37830" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{2,0,1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427377} {:answer/id #uuid "cfdc823e-90d7-5645-a8fc-5def08fa694a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{2,4,0\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427381} {:answer/id #uuid "ed7b9e7c-c2fe-5559-be97-bb8125d6fa51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-1,2,0\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427382}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0fde5085-a635-5696-9cd7-100b3c72cad2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-1,4,1\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427374} :answer-field/id #uuid "0da5b7ce-3185-5f7f-9a0f-797454d122c3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186427384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2ffb7e93-f33c-5adf-acf0-f55e6fbbb059" :question/math-academy-id "q-36831" :question/problem "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=4,$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=1.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are always the entries on the main diagonal."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125017 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124522 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "289ae874-f555-50ee-896f-eb2188004124" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 3x3 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34b63fae-2f7c-5fe2-a1a4-0ec3c381a3dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -4)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321550} {:answer/id #uuid "7e0eb44e-ac21-5b2a-a972-1f77bba194b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda +4)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322140} {:answer/id #uuid "9bb97b3b-8054-574a-8ea2-ed4ef42cb19d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -10)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322378} {:answer/id #uuid "d58e6bae-778a-5650-bdd1-f71c17fa7409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -16)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322813} {:answer/id #uuid "d90d6023-7a0f-5e73-af24-24eac2a1b5b0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-16)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322849}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d58e6bae-778a-5650-bdd1-f71c17fa7409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -16)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322813} :answer-field/id #uuid "55997a27-4ab4-5568-9f4a-ccc1b73a2faf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323333}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2accab64-f6f1-5300-b0aa-a3471aee3ef9" :question/math-academy-id "q-36845" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-3-\\lambda  & 2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $3$rd row, we obtain the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-3-\\lambda  & 2 & -1 \\\\ 5 & 2-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-3-\\lambda  & 2 \\\\ 5 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )((-3-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-2\\cdot 5) & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -16) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447465 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124571 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef311af0-0e95-5574-a151-2971ad66bd08" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 4x4 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "040615ac-cb0a-5fce-99f6-4ed63d75aaeb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -5)(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447376} {:answer/id #uuid "2498f497-cc93-5d6b-a1c8-83b43853b063" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +5)(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447388} {:answer/id #uuid "26c14220-eceb-59a1-9b09-b87b97b8a7b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -5)(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447389} {:answer/id #uuid "2cd374ea-5661-54f0-b4f0-721321849bb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -5)(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda +1)^{2}=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447391} {:answer/id #uuid "f9560526-e72e-5f8b-ab9e-5ebe403d5441" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -5)(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -1)^{2}=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447448}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "26c14220-eceb-59a1-9b09-b87b97b8a7b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -5)(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447389} :answer-field/id #uuid "834cc150-7558-5f94-8ad6-94ae5f3cfbc7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447457}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "243cda6a-277e-5555-a0d1-a4b1a66521e4" :question/math-academy-id "q-37353" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -3 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 4-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & -3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (5-\\lambda )(-1-\\lambda )(4-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -5)(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -4)(\\lambda -1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323904 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124522 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "289ae874-f555-50ee-896f-eb2188004124" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 3x3 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c03b0d6-311f-55a2-81e5-71e742dd7ac5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -2)({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +10)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321359} {:answer/id #uuid "1c6d5a60-4a1c-585b-9c6a-c38aad8c908f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +3)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -3)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321363} {:answer/id #uuid "865a1300-13a1-5889-ab1b-b6361dc737c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -1)^{2}(\\lambda +2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322214} {:answer/id #uuid "92792d5d-eeb6-5848-b334-bcfc0d1701dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +2)({\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda -10)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322309} {:answer/id #uuid "a6d6efdd-902a-5ff9-acb4-e7d10dff1a1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +2)({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +10)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322452}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6d6efdd-902a-5ff9-acb4-e7d10dff1a1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +2)({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +10)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322452} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a26514d-bab5-54f6-affd-0baea61f5deb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323220}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a0e8e60c-423d-5778-945d-945b43ca8811" :question/math-academy-id "q-37354" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $2$nd row, we obtain the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & -2-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -3 & 5 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-2-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ -3 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-2-\\lambda )((1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-(3)(-3)) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +2)({\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +10) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447470 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124522 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "289ae874-f555-50ee-896f-eb2188004124" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 3x3 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "527cb312-c6a6-5a5d-9bcf-61787139c3d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda (\\lambda +10)(\\lambda -20)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447402} {:answer/id #uuid "6561688f-0f5b-5532-a636-4e1b1e285d0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +40)(\\lambda -6)(\\lambda -30)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447408} {:answer/id #uuid "6e034595-10dd-5a5a-8870-372a9c9d5b27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{2}(\\lambda +10)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447412} {:answer/id #uuid "beaaed4b-e3bf-59ab-9162-b63b3f77485b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -10)(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +20)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447436} {:answer/id #uuid "d221a7d6-bd60-5f61-a4eb-8f48bc286186" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +80)(\\lambda -14)(\\lambda -60)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "527cb312-c6a6-5a5d-9bcf-61787139c3d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda (\\lambda +10)(\\lambda -20)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447402} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4136c8d-5a3d-54a3-8e0e-9880d33a4256" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447459}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "a82c548a-99d5-5982-b67f-c8bf62fc70fb" :question/math-academy-id "q-37357" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-40 & 6 & 30 \\\\ 0 & -10 & 0 \\\\ -80 & 14 & 60\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-40-\\lambda  & 6 & 30 \\\\ 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -80 & 14 & 60-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $2$nd row, we obtain the following:  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-40-\\lambda  & 6 & 30 \\\\ 0 & -10-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ -80 & 14 & 60-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-10-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}-40-\\lambda  & 30 \\\\ -80 & 60-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-10-\\lambda )((-40-\\lambda )(60-\\lambda )-(30)(-80)) & =0 \\\\ (-10-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-20\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +10)(\\lambda )(\\lambda -20) & =0 \\\\ \\lambda (\\lambda +10)(\\lambda -20) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323910 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124523 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5abea3ab-76a7-5598-8ede-b4cf88dd47d7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Eigenvalues of a General 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4c92bdd9-561f-50f8-a0af-b026acb7e7d2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -52=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321751} {:answer/id #uuid "679f1b6a-bb22-58ad-9008-20f76acaf14c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-10{\\lambda }^{2}+43\\lambda -90=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321955} {:answer/id #uuid "688684d9-f540-59a5-826c-2faac539f6c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}+7{\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda -48=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186321961} {:answer/id #uuid "a6e445b9-3e7b-5df5-8de9-a07b0a91fd34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda +6=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322453} {:answer/id #uuid "c8f0d0d9-d2ec-529d-bfe9-31a08f8548aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+49\\lambda -138=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a6e445b9-3e7b-5df5-8de9-a07b0a91fd34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda +6=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186322453} :answer-field/id #uuid "b4874765-573f-531a-bb89-b09ddf9d2051" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186323521}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4b421cae-1cc2-5e38-a509-6349aee206e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-37394" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -8 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 8 & 3 \\\\ -6 & -10 & -3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & -8 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 8-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ -6 & -10 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & -8 & -4 \\\\ 3 & 8-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ -6 & -10 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}8-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ -10 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-(-8)|\\begin{aligned}3 & 3 \\\\ -6 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|+(-4)|\\begin{aligned}3 & 8-\\lambda  \\\\ -6 & -10\\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}-5\\lambda +6)+8(-3\\lambda +9)-4(-6\\lambda +18) & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -6)+(-24\\lambda +72)-(-24\\lambda +72) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}+4{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -6 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}-4{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda +6 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366013 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124523 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5abea3ab-76a7-5598-8ede-b4cf88dd47d7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Eigenvalues of a General 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2fd702e4-330a-55c4-a31c-c235740df973" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}-109\\lambda +470=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366015} {:answer/id #uuid "1bc53b3d-fa24-5966-986f-e002765bf747" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}-31\\lambda +32=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366016} {:answer/id #uuid "7fb400bf-02c7-5b7d-be66-3597e2682ca1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}-10\\lambda -5=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366017} {:answer/id #uuid "d4b97459-5f9c-583d-bbf4-79230e9fff2f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}-109\\lambda +110=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366018} {:answer/id #uuid "4587a64e-a88f-55cb-a42a-0f3b6f625361" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda +2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4587a64e-a88f-55cb-a42a-0f3b6f625361" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda +2=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366019} :answer-field/id #uuid "23f37a83-a62e-50f1-affa-75b650e2059a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366014}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "94bfabe8-f33f-5580-888f-0bac595dc86b" :question/math-academy-id "q-37395" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 & -6 \\\\ 4 & 5 & -12 \\\\ 3 & 3 & -7\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,C-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nC-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 3 & -6 \\\\ 4 & 5-\\lambda  & -12 \\\\ 3 & 3 & -7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(C-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(C-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}4-\\lambda  & 3 & -6 \\\\ 4 & 5-\\lambda  & -12 \\\\ 3 & 3 & -7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}5-\\lambda  & -12 \\\\ 3 & -7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-3|\\begin{aligned}4 & -12 \\\\ 3 & -7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|+(-6)|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5-\\lambda  \\\\ 3 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (4-\\lambda )({\\lambda }^{2}+2\\lambda +1)-3(-4\\lambda +8)-6(-3+3\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}+7\\lambda +4)-(-12\\lambda +24)-(-18+18\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}+2{\\lambda }^{2}+\\lambda -2 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}-2{\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda +2 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447472 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124522 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "289ae874-f555-50ee-896f-eb2188004124" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 3x3 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dd806b5-b00a-5419-b12d-acd06881a066" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{3,4,-5\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447379} {:answer/id #uuid "81325892-1923-5229-ade2-a096f5c023d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-3,0,3\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447420} {:answer/id #uuid "8d939250-f6e6-5ac0-9745-e9c2d7ddd5e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-3,-4,5\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447424} {:answer/id #uuid "978f7fe8-15da-52c6-ba65-b60baa2efb75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{0,-4,-2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447427} {:answer/id #uuid "c32cb1b1-29a5-5579-8622-98540b8194df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-3,-2,5\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447437}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8d939250-f6e6-5ac0-9745-e9c2d7ddd5e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-3,-4,5\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447424} :answer-field/id #uuid "b75011bd-dfba-5826-af46-a8b32028e02b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447460}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bca3e3e8-22f6-5c69-8cd2-18d06e6e998f" :question/math-academy-id "q-80553" :question/problem "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,B-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nB-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-3-\\lambda  & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(B-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(B-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-3-\\lambda  & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -4-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-3-\\lambda )(-4-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +3)(\\lambda +4)(\\lambda -5) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-3,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-4,$ and ${\\lambda }_{3}=5.$\n\n**Note:** The eigenvalues of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix are always the entries on the main diagonal."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186404128 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124523 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5abea3ab-76a7-5598-8ede-b4cf88dd47d7" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Eigenvalues of a General 3x3 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35af3a4a-7335-5fe9-967e-58adf4f90f66" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-1,2\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447393} {:answer/id #uuid "5224fac3-9456-54c5-8164-7b956ad4457d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-1,2,-3\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447401} {:answer/id #uuid "583a945a-8104-5e57-8cc3-097d8e920823" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{1,-6\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447404} {:answer/id #uuid "bda8e9d4-016c-519c-908c-da427a5c28c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-1,-2,3\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447434} {:answer/id #uuid "be3f9e84-b89f-56ff-858a-b9716e9565bd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{2,-3\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447435}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bda8e9d4-016c-519c-908c-da427a5c28c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\lambda \\in \\{-1,-2,3\\}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447434} :answer-field/id #uuid "135ac5a3-acd1-57d7-85af-ac59d7bb8214" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404129}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ba3b9cc6-841d-5636-9777-0bc1e8c24e7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-80825" :question/problem "Determine all real eigenvalues $\\lambda $ of the matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is given by $det(A-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nExpanding the determinant across the $1$st row, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-{\\lambda }^{3}+6\\lambda +5)-(-1-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ -{\\lambda }^{3}+7\\lambda +6 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{3}-7\\lambda -6 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we need to solve this equation. We find the first root by testing some values. According to the rational zeros theorem, a list of good first guesses consists of all divisors of $6:$ \n\n$$\n\\pm 1,\\pm 2,\\pm 3,\\pm 6\n$$\n\n- Let's pick $x=1.$ Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(1)^{3}-7(1)-6 & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =1$ is not a root of the equation.\n\n- Let's pick $x=-1.$ Substituting to the characteristic equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1)^{3}-7(-1)-6 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $\\lambda =-1$ is a root of the equation.\n\nSo, we can factor $(\\lambda +1)$ out of ${\\lambda }^{3}-7\\lambda -6$ using synthetic division:\n\n| $-1$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-7$ | $-6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $↓$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $6$ |\n|  | $1$ | $-1$ | $-6$ | $0$ |\n\nSo, we obtain the following factorization:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(\\lambda +1)({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -6) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}=-1,$ $\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-2,\\,$ and $\\,{\\lambda }_{3}=3.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354507 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124571 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef311af0-0e95-5574-a151-2971ad66bd08" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 4x4 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "242bc1ff-9d6a-5249-9c87-df81d32a7785" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda -2)(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +3)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186351897} {:answer/id #uuid "4ca0ab54-3950-52f9-9f8a-4d77319ad175" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -3)^{2}(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352267} {:answer/id #uuid "4fbc21b4-be4d-543a-b434-958a7eefccf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +3)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352287} {:answer/id #uuid "c609ae85-57e2-57a3-9e3e-63455f2e5cd6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -3)^{2}(\\lambda -2)(\\lambda -1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353284} {:answer/id #uuid "ea8f1d9a-964d-5721-a11c-a90ebcc3202e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +{3}^{2})(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -1)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186353612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fbc21b4-be4d-543a-b434-958a7eefccf3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +3)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186352287} :answer-field/id #uuid "709448bf-2e7d-5b59-85e2-71d9ceccca7a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354027}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f5c38096-9f20-5f16-82a1-f8397b703a46" :question/math-academy-id "q-86749" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$P=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,P-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nP-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2-\\lambda  & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda  & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(P-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(P-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3-\\lambda  & 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2-\\lambda  & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1-\\lambda  & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (3-\\lambda )(-2-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )(-3-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -3)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186447473 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124571 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef311af0-0e95-5574-a151-2971ad66bd08" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 4x4 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09eda0ec-8e1b-5e11-a68f-03dfb4b379e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -7)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447378} {:answer/id #uuid "7638f82e-310a-5356-96a6-5573794cce10" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda +1)(\\lambda -2)(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda +2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447416} {:answer/id #uuid "d612d7a1-320d-5230-8d43-429cf1f224b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -7)(\\lambda -2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447443} {:answer/id #uuid "e44519c4-103d-5ede-bc2f-bccaf86b7bee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda -2)^{2}(\\lambda -7)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447445} {:answer/id #uuid "f3ff7a34-01f9-5d59-a7ea-85ad5c394bee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +2)^{2}(\\lambda -7)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447447}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d612d7a1-320d-5230-8d43-429cf1f224b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -7)(\\lambda -2)=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447443} :answer-field/id #uuid "506939ed-7e7a-58fe-a23e-568138385abc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186447453}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d00c6bd7-a884-5180-8cfd-0ffa34fc590f" :question/math-academy-id "q-86751" :question/problem "Find the characteristic equation of the matrix \n$E=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 7 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,E-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nE-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -2-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 7-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(E-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nSince the determinant of a triangular (or diagonal) matrix is given by the product of the entries on the main diagonal, we obtain the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(E-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -2-\\lambda  & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 7-\\lambda  & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 4 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(-2-\\lambda )(7-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda ) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda -1)(\\lambda +2)(\\lambda -7)(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366511 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124571 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef311af0-0e95-5574-a151-2971ad66bd08" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Eigenvalues of a 4x4 Matrix Containing a Block of Zeros"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "840ca690-b2c9-5b7f-b15f-c9d055dd8d15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366513} {:answer/id #uuid "a7ad9017-9c8c-5cf4-9483-8848e227dc5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366514} {:answer/id #uuid "8b5ac16e-45f2-53e9-a50c-fa437e5c9bf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366515} {:answer/id #uuid "7c955f28-72f9-5a22-baa1-4d21191b888f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366516} {:answer/id #uuid "012e35f8-4aac-5831-9df6-9441a06202a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366517}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "840ca690-b2c9-5b7f-b15f-c9d055dd8d15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I, II, and III" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366513} :answer-field/id #uuid "5d0a6690-f84d-58f7-85b3-ab37c4b399d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366512}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5ad99f7f-a225-5eb9-a085-4dc337f7e2b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-86752" :question/problem "$$\nD=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nConsider the matrix $D$ given above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\lambda =2$ is an eigenvalue of $D$\n\nII. $\\lambda =-1$ is an eigenvalue of $D$\n\nIII. The eigenvalue $\\lambda =-1$ has algebraic multiplicity $2$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the matrix $\\,D-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nD-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & -2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1-\\lambda  & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThe characteristic equation is $det(D-\\lambda I)=0.$ \n\nNotice that we can expand the $4\\times 4$ determinant across the $1$st column, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(D-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}-1-\\lambda  & -2 & 4 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 1-\\lambda  & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & -\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -\\lambda  & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -7-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, expanding the $3\\times 3$ determinant across the $3$rd row, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(-1-\\lambda )(-7-\\lambda )|\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ -2 & -\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (-1-\\lambda )(-7-\\lambda )((1-\\lambda )(-\\lambda )-2) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +7)({\\lambda }^{2}-\\lambda -2) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda -2)(\\lambda +1) & =0 \\\\ (\\lambda +1)^{2}(\\lambda +7)(\\lambda -2) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the eigenvalues of $D$ are $\\lambda =-1$ (with algebraic multiplicity $2$), $\\lambda =-7$ and $\\lambda =2.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III.\""}]}
